  <!-- Column 4 Text -->
  <div slot="col-4-text">
    <p>
      large mountain of toys there. <br />
      ‘Book your Holidays’ <br />
      Far different from days when I was young <br />
      We still worked here on Christmas Day
    </p>

    <p>
      In Scotland there were no holidays then <br />
      till we stopped off on Hogmanay <br />
      Things gradually changed after the war years <br />
      Soon more breaks became common place
    </p>

    <p>
      But the true meaning of this festive month <br />
      has gone without leaving a trace <br />
      It could be the result of modern traits <br />
      Living the fast life never stopping a minute
    </p>

    <p>
      There’s so much out there every day <br />
      To see and do and cram in it <br />
      No time to ponder, relax and reflect <br />
      As the years keep speeding on their way
    </p>

    <p>
      Still grasping at the Earthly pleasures <br />
      Lacking the Celestial joy of Christmas Day <br />
      Eila’s December Reflections	Eila’s December Reflections	Eila’s December Reflections	Eila’s December Reflections <br />
      Far different from days when I was young
    </p>

    <p>
      We still worked here on Christmas Day; <br />
      In Scotland there were no holidays then <br />
      till we stopped off on Hogmanay. <br />
      Things gradually changed after the war years
    </p>

